From ae957dfb89ad2aa0198c9dfaf7d8b3e870f0c78b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LightCraft additional extensions <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:24:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Module bar (Library | Develop | Print | Export) and a
 full-window Print module
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Library and Develop map onto the photo grid and the detail view with the
Edit panel; Print shows the print settings and page preview in the window;
Export opens the Export dialog. The bar folds into one drop-down when the
window is too narrow for it and the search field. Module keys follow
Lightroom Classic (Cmd+Alt+1/2/6) and the Window menu lists the modules.

Print > Photo Size > Size by long edge (default 10 in) lays out one centred
cell per selected photo (at most 50) through the print.* commands, with no
package border, and names the photos it leaves out. The print layout it
replaces is given back when the module closes or the option is turned off,
so File > Print prints the current selection again; page setup and print
job changes made in the module stay. Arrow keys turn the module's pages,
view and panel commands and Esc leave it, and File > Print closes it first.

Print labels get their own translation context (zh-Hans: 纸张, 纵向/横向)
and the print settings are translated into Simplified and Traditional
Chinese.
